Hi Anna,
&nbsp;
On Alicia’s witness statement, below are our and Giles Wheeler KC’s final comments:
&nbsp;

Para. 6:
 add “and” after “NOx legal case team,”.
&nbsp;

Para. 13:
 in the final line, replace “which may imperil” with “from”.
&nbsp;

Para. 17:
 replace “Mercedes GLO” with “Lead GLO”.
&nbsp;

Para. 22:
 Each of the Lead Cases have individual agency agreements.
&nbsp;

Para. 35 (responding to your comment at para. 28):
 Add new sub-paragraph “Mr Gallagher: I acknowledge that the Firm is in a dispute with Mr Gallagher and, accordingly, pending the resolution of that dispute, the Firm must be cautious in what it says about Mr Gallagher. However, the Firm rejects the
 allegations attributed to Mr Gallagher concerning the nature of the relationship between Pogust Goodhead and Gramercy.”
&nbsp;

Para. 37.1:
 should be “these” (not “this”) facilities.
&nbsp;

Para. 37.3:
 change “peripheral” to “some”.
&nbsp;

Para. 43:
 change “filed today” to “filed yesterday”.
&nbsp;
If you wish to do this by consent, the draft documents will need to be sent to the Defendants as soon as possible
 this morning and ask them to consent today.&nbsp; We suggest being conciliatory in this request – recognising it is not much time – but giving a deadline of 4.30/5pm.

Relatedly, I understand that Jess and Xenia are working together on finalising the exhibit.
&nbsp;
Kind regards,
James
