Dear all,


I hope you are well.


&nbsp;


I write to provide you with a brief update now we have concluded the opening week of the trial.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


Monday and Tuesday were for the Claimants to provide their opening submissions to the Court on the Lead Cases, while Wednesday and Thursday were and are for
 each of the Defendants to provide their response. Ford was covered across Monday and Tuesday morning by the Claimants, and then the Ford Defendants made their response on Wednesday. &nbsp;


&nbsp;


In relation to Ford - our take on the openings is that all of the Defendants were taken aback by how strongly we put the case to Ford. We do not think they
 expected for us to so aggressively put Ford at the front and centre in our opening and would have instead been prepared for us to instead turn our attention to some of the other Defendants. Our counsel team put on screen a number of extremely damaging documents,
 which various of the press and NGOs who were in attendance also took note of. These documents included internal emails between Ford employees where they discussed updates to improve the vehicles in circumstances where they were considered to be in the worse
 20% of vehicles in the EU. Similarly, we also displayed Ford internal presentations showing how test results which were above regulatory limits, were in fact &quot;in line with Ford's expectations&quot;. The Court looked interested in these documents


&nbsp;


Ford's response we have opined was a little underwhelming, focusing on how Ford self-profess to be industry standard bearers for compliance and how the Claimants
 have not appropriately set out our case, while failing to deal with the more damaging information, something which we believe the Judge acutely noticed. We also ensured that our mechanical expert, Mr Carder, was in attendance yesterday so he is more familiar
 with the court layout in advance of his attendance for examination and cross examination.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


The summary is that there were no &quot;rabbit out of a hat&quot; reveals from any of the Defendants and the trial will roll onto next week with things having not markedly
 shifted this week.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


