&nbsp;


The most important point here is to make sure that what is said about PG’s funding agreements is accurate and not misleading by omission, because anything that isn’t quite right (or a relevant funding arrangement
 not included) will doubtless be seized on down the line.


&nbsp;


On the ATE assumptions, my views are as follows (and I know these are shared by Simon):


&nbsp;




We think that future costs for ADR and Experts should be included in the relevant expenditure calculations. Despite not having been assessed by the court yet, those costs would be incurred within the relevant period and therefore will be taken into account
 when assessing of sufficiency of cover. It would be reasonable at this stage to take the Claimants’ offers against those phases as the starting point for what we say is required, but we must recognise that leaving those phases out altogether isn’t going to
