 (and additional cover) if the position on ATE sufficiency is to be maintained before the court.




&nbsp;




Similarly, we don’t think there is a strong case for downgrading the % of incurred costs by 10%. Again, if this is to go into the letter we ought to treat it internally as a holding position while you look to increase cover.


&nbsp;


We agree that it is not sensible to disclose in the letter that you are looking to increase cover. Most importantly, that essentially amounts to a concession that what you have is insufficient - and additionally,
 as you point out, you may not be able to secure further cover and we don’t want to box ourselves in.


