Unknown - I haven't played a role in Vauxhall.




On my cases at least, I provide them with monthly updates. On top of those updates, I will also contact them for instructions on items such as discontinuances or material updates.




On the expert applications, I advised them of the applications, but did not take their instructions on the actual content of the application. The key reason for this was due to the confidential
 nature of the expert reports - the CComs haven't seen the reports yet, becuase they have confidential information and they are not CRO members. They would therefore be unable to advise on what should be kept or removed from the reports.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


Given the material change to the Litigation that us stepping down as Lead Sols will have, and the change in PGs role (and therefore the CComs roles) in the
 Litigation, this strikes me as a classic time when we need to a) advise them of why we are doing this and b) take their instructions on doing so.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


