 the Litigaiton, but we can't just set that to the side. We can't continue to let our clients think we are &quot;running&quot; the Litigation when we are not. I think that risks 1.4 COC.


&nbsp;


As a bare minimum we need to advise them of a) and long before they hear of it in the press. To actively deny them this information (and to not take instructions)
 strikes me as a route that we should not consider going down. I suppose we could always run it past counsel (maybe Friston?) to get a seal of approval.


