What do you think @Neil Pigott? So long as we’re not going to in anyway misrep the current situation?&nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 18:49To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; 'Neil Pigott' &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alessia de Quincey &lt;alessia.dequincey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Insurance analysis&nbsp;Thanks Alicia.&nbsp;@pallas the sentence below was meant to lay the groundwork for communicating additional changes to insurers. Do we need to revisit this?&nbsp;‘We will provide a more detailed response outlining further upcoming changes within the case teams, ensuring you have a clear understanding of the updated structure’.&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 18:20To: 'Neil Pigott' &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alessia de Quincey &lt;alessia.dequincey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Insurance analysis&nbsp;I think this is now fine. By mentioning Mike and not the others, is this problematic in terms of full disclosure? &nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 17:56To: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alessia de Quincey &lt;alessia.dequincey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Insurance analysis&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Helena,&nbsp;On our side the highlighted sentence mentioning Pallas is to come out, please, as discussed by Natasha and Alicia.&nbsp;There is one small addition marked to the added paragraph under Lead Solicitor.&nbsp;Best regards,&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;Pigott​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1005|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;75&nbsp;5741&nbsp;2828E:&nbsp;&nbsp;neil.pigott@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 17:45To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alessia de Quincey &lt;Alessia.deQuincey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Insurance analysis&nbsp;Hi all, &nbsp;See draft email below for WTW incorporating Michael’s resignation and the Lead solicitor point. &nbsp;Changes to the previous draft are highlighted. &nbsp;Grateful for your comments. &nbsp;Thanks Helena -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&nbsp;Hi James,&nbsp;Many thanks for your email. &nbsp;We acknowledge there has been a delay in sharing recent updates. Due to confidentiality requirements surrounding ongoing internal discussions, we were unable to communicate certain developments sooner.&nbsp;Please find below latest developments regarding NOx and responses to Ignite’s queries.&nbsp;Lead Solicitor&nbsp;The Firm has in consultation with the other Lead Solicitor and subject to the Court’s approval decided to step down temporarily as Lead Solicitor in the lead cases.&nbsp; This will obviate any attempt by the Defendants to distract the proceedings tactically by (unmerited) references to our personnel/legal team changes.&nbsp; The firm remains a fully active member of the Steering Committee, and is in the process of agreeing mechanisms whereby it can continue work on the matter in substantive terms. We do not anticipate material financial impact on the conduct of the proceedings.We address Ignite’s questions and the questions about Tom Goodhead in your email of today below. &nbsp;Response to insurer queries &nbsp;Key Personal/Lead Lawyers - per the verbal request can the lead lawyers per NOx manufacturer and for the BHP matter be detailed to us please?&nbsp; The board of directors now comprises Alicia Alinia, Howard Morris, and Joseph Moreno as directors of both the Parent and the Firm (the “Board”). Thomas Goodhead has now left both as CEO and Director of the Firm.&nbsp; The Board is responsible for the overall management of the Firm, and each member of the Board has statutory duties to exercise independent judgment in accordance with the Companies Act 2006.The Board appointments demonstrate that Pogust Goodhead is being run by an extremely experienced and committed team of independent, regulated, legal professionals. Each of the Board members is regulated by the SRA and qualified to practice in England &amp; Wales.Following Pete’s departure, Anna Varga, whom you have met, has taken the lead on Mercedes and Vauxhall cases and is overall supervisor for the remaining NOx cases. Working closely with our case leads, Anna will ensure a smooth transition and maintain consistency in how the cases are managed. [For BHP our case leads are Guy Robson and Faranak Ghajavand].&nbsp;Additionally, we are delighted to have engaged one of the market’s leading litigation practices [Pallas Partners], to work alongside us on the emissions cases providing access to senior level strategic legal advice for liability and quantum workstreams. Craig Shuttleworth (Kastle Solicitors and previously Head of Litigation at Jones Day), who has decades of litigation experience is also joining us as a strategic advisor on emissions. Craig has been working with the firm supporting BHP and other matters since 2023[, and will work to support teams across both the NOx and BHP matters].&nbsp;We want to reassure you that the cases continue to receive the level of expertise and attention required. Our retained barristers and partner firms remain fully engaged and unchanged, providing continuity and stability in external representation. Internally, the team continues to operate with the senior oversight and leadership necessary to progress the cases effectively. We are confident that this structure offers the strongest platform for achieving a successful outcomeWe can confirm that Mr Burke has formally tendered his resignation with Pogust Goodhead and is currently working his notice period. We will liaise with the Defendants in those Litigations to advise them accordingly. We will provide a more detailed response outlining further upcoming changes within the case teams, ensuring you have a clear understanding of the updated structure.&nbsp;Negotiating Partners - should they differ from 1, can the lawyers in charge of WP negotiations also be detailed to us please?&nbsp;These individuals are consistent with those mentioned above.&nbsp;Recent Costs Judgment - Last week a costs Judgment was published which saw the claimants budget reduced significantly for the trial. Does this cause any issues for PG and/or Gramercy? link: https://caselaw.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ewhc/kb/2025/2307The reductions that the court applied to the Quantum Trial budgets related mainly to costs submitted by non-lead claimant firms. The reductions applied to PG related costs were relatively modest 30% after adjusting for non-lead claimant firm costs. This 30% reduction is modest both in the context of expected recoverable costs on success, and in the context of budget to adequately resource the case. Therefore, PG does not consider there to be any material effect on PG or Gramercy. Gramercy have also not raised any material concern.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal informati