As Signature's draft application points out at 8(b)(iii) - a letter was sent out yesterday, naming me as the PG contact.&nbsp;




That I am named as the contact appears to have been an administrative oversight, and I put no blame on the sender of the letter, however this has now lead to a misleading position, or what will be a mislead position if not immediately clarified, underpinning
 the concerns I had regarding paragraph 27 of the letter sent to the Defendants on Tuesday 23 September (see my email at 12.52 today and my suggestion at 15.59 on 23 September).&nbsp;




The SRA Code of Conduct at 1.4 says &quot;You do not mislead or attempt to mislead your
clients,
 the court&nbsp;or
 others, either by your own acts or omissions or allowing or being complicit in the acts or omissions of others (including your
client)&quot;




